name issue_453_h264_missing_packets_high_jitter
describe high_jitter with the SPS/PPS tracker and the packet buffer's H.264 missing-packets hold on: the delta frames after a dropped IDR start wait for the next keyframe instead of drawing a second keyframe request, as libwebrtc (issue #453)
# libwebrtc's PacketBuffer::FindFrames (modules/video_coding/packet_buffer.cc) hands out an H.264 frame without an
# IDR only when no earlier sequence number is missing (missing_packets_, UpdateMissingPackets). The IDR start that
# H264SpsPpsTracker dropped stays missing, so the deltas after it never reach RtpVideoStreamReceiver2::OnAssembledFrame
# and its first-frame-delta keyframe request is not sent. Seed 3, libwebrtc (parity-data compare-webrtc.json):
# time to first frame 469 ms, 1 keyframe request. Ours: tracker alone 453 ms / 2 requests; with the hold 453 ms / 1.
# 10 seeds (1-10), ours tracker alone / both / libwebrtc: keyframe requests 1.8 / 1.2 / 1.2 (equal to libwebrtc on
# 10 of 10 seeds with both); time to first frame 449 / 449 / 433 ms.
duration 30s
seed 3
sps_pps_tracker on
h264_missing_packets on
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=30ms jitter=40ms reorder=on queue=300ms
expect video.time_to_first_frame_ms > 400
expect video.keyframe_requests == 1
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect audio.concealed_pct < 2
